## Reviewer's findings

An independent reviewer read the spec without the draft and found values that
look unnecessary or too complex. These are values you proposed yourself (with
PROPOSED/SUGGESTION marks); the author's values are not here and must stay
exactly as they are.

~~~yaml
{{ findings }}
~~~

For each finding, either apply it — remove, simplify or merge the value as
proposed, keeping its mark — or keep the value and explain in `notes` why it's
needed (`kind: uncertain`, `field` — the finding's path). The reviewer doesn't
know the draft: if the draft asks for the value, keep it and say so. Change
nothing beyond these findings: every value without a mark must stay unchanged.
